From: Kumar Ankit <186563577+krank-09@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:41:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] feat: plain-language explanations of audit records via
 Gemini

Adds an Explain button next to every audit record link (admin feed, incidents, Bob and Charlie terminals). It opens a dialog with a short Gemini-written summary for non-specialists. GET /api/audit/{id}/explain applies the same access rules as the record itself and sends only the evidence-stripped record. Key read from GEMINI_API_KEY (server-side, header not URL); model from GEMINI_MODEL; responses cached per record; no new dependencies. Without a key the dialog says the feature is off and still links the signed JSON.
